{
 "scope": "L13: weighted coarea for locally Lipschitz functions, a common and strict generalization of L11 and L12. One new theorem; no hole migrated. The log-concave Cheeger-Buser line was handed to collaborator Wang Haocheng on 2026-09-16 and is deliberately untouched.",
 "head": "dcc158d7d3b9e91f17d2ee0fd49b30cdb6f4f7d8",
 "origin_main": "dcc158d7d3b9e91f17d2ee0fd49b30cdb6f4f7d8",
 "incoming_receipt": "build/verification/20260916T081142.821228Z/report.json",
 "incoming_snapshot": "115a7e19375062d43882a1ff2caa16b5ca52b0791af25734aacfff66ac61735c",
 "incoming_entries": 495,
 "incoming_status": "passed",
 "new_theorem": "FunctionalInequalities.KLS.coarea_of_locallyLipschitz",
 "hypotheses": {
  "on_u": "LocallyLipschitz u only",
  "on_S": "MeasurableSet S, otherwise arbitrary; may be unbounded and of infinite volume",
  "on_g": "Measurable g : V -> ENNReal, may be identically infinity",
  "not_assumed": [
   "global Lipschitz constant",
   "C1 regularity",
   "boundedness",
   "finite volume",
   "integrability",
   "regular values",
   "positive dimension",
   "SFinite surface measure"
  ],
  "surfaceMeasure_normalization_unchanged": true
 },
 "generalization": {
  "recovers_L12": "LipschitzWith K u -> LocallyLipschitz u; audited by recovers_L12, which does not name coarea_of_lipschitz",
  "recovers_L11": "ContDiff R 1 u -> LocallyLipschitz u; audited by recovers_L11, which does not name coarea_of_contDiff",
  "L11_and_L12_statements_unchanged": true,
  "restated_through_L13": false,
  "compatibility_alias_added": false,
  "strictness_witness": "fun x : R => x ^ 2 + norm x",
  "witness_locallyLipschitz_proved": true,
  "witness_not_globally_lipschitz_proved": true,
  "witness_not_differentiableAt_zero_proved": true
 },
 "proof_outline": [
  "half-open annuli ball 0 (k+1) \\ ball 0 k: disjoint, measurable, covering by floor of the norm",
  "finite-dimensional hence proper: LocallyLipschitzOn.exists_lipschitzOnWith_of_compact on each closed ball",
  "LipschitzOnWith.extend_real (McShane) gives a globally Lipschitz representative v k there",
  "each piece lies in the OPEN ball, so u and v k agree on a neighbourhood of every point: EventuallyEq.gradient_eq gives pointwise gradient equality and the level sets cut the piece identically",
  "L12 on each piece, then lintegral_iUnion and lintegral_tsum over the disjoint pieces",
  "total slice AEMeasurable by the same countable decomposition plus AEMeasurable.tsum, because an unbounded S carries no global LipschitzOnWith bound so L5 does not apply directly"
 ],
